id: pm-web-sblf
title: Coverage configuration failures leave stale accepted reports
description: "The coverage gate invalidates reports after configuration parsing and source enumeration. A missing configured source or malformed manifest therefore leaves an older successful LCOV receipt in place. Move invalidation before any configuration read and verify the actual gate in a disposable package: passing report, failing source inventory, then no accepted artifacts."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-05T05:22:24.137Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-05T05:54:50.540Z"
author: codex-sol
estimated_minutes: 60
acceptance_criteria: Configuration and source failures clear all accepted coverage reports and actual gate subprocess tests enforce statements and unloaded-file accounting.
comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-05T05:36:40.300Z",codex-sol,"Real subprocess gate tests pass 2/2: independently enforced statement threshold, unloaded executable source at zero coverage, successful fresh reports, failure invalidation and missing-metric rejection. Invalidation now runs before manifest/config/source validation, so a failed inventory cannot preserve an old accepted report. The gate owns an isolated c8 counter/report directory and never publishes failed-run artifacts."
  "2026-10-05T05:53:18.396Z",codex-sol,"The actual gate subprocess regression passes both cases: successful fresh receipt publication, untouched module inclusion at zero, independent statements rejection, missing metric rejection, and configuration/source failures clearing accepted evidence. Linked pm test passes. Full 487-test suite also passes at the ratcheted four-metric floors."
